 @Crackalacking_Z   No need for an FPS cap? So you just play with massive screen tearing when you go over your monitor's refresh rate? Basically everyone plays with some form of an FPS cap nowadays.

What's the power consumption in Furmark? Power consumption in games varies wildly. If it's even stable. According to google people can only go as low as 1000Mv without losing performance. 930Mv while gaining performance sounds like BS, that's a massive difference.

Something's not right here. Either you only play basically the same game and it happens to be stable there, or you are losing significant performance without realizing it. The fact that you claim to play without an FPS cap is a red flag. For example, enabling nvidia Reflex automatically imposes an FPS cap. V-Sync is also an FPS cap. And without an FPS cap you'd often be playing without G-sync which is pretty bad.

 @imo098765  It can be tricky

One thing I noticed in the past is that there's sometimes a trap/sprial for PC components. "Okay, if I push $20, I get a lot more. Oh... now if I push another $20-30, there's the next tier... Um... okay, I should cut back a bit because I went from $100 to $200"

You can push, then another push, then another and the price just keeps sliding up. Being a former budget PC gamer, having to try to figure out the best bang for the buck could be really trick and I had to emotionally calm myself at times

